      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would completely change the game, an absolute must. I am really happy with their recent implementation of data persistence but, imagine what one could do with that AND dynamic URLs. \n\nI would love to have my own webserver for users to send and retrieve information securely, you could even transfer config or game information across multiple worlds effortlessly for the user.\n\nI'm imagining entire communities evolving from this. You can foresee evil coming from this too, like hooking into central economies across many instances based on real money, controlling people for profit. But just say that's not allowed, add it to the report menu. \n\nThere is reason for why they'd hesitate to include such an implementation, but as ArcaneBlackwood suggested, an additional setting for \"Allow dynamic URL's\" or perhaps a prompt upon joining, and a slightly expanded TOS would wrap it all up.\n\nPlease! Share this around! <3",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
